## Check the implementation

Test images disabled, narrow screens, enlarged text and reading order. Supply dimensions to reduce layout movement and keep images responsive without cropping important details.

Use the [civica.uk accessibility checks](../accessibility/testing.html) and compare the rendered result in light and dark modes, Vivid and Muted tones, and at 320 CSS pixels. The example markup is a starting point; a theme alone does not add its application logic.

## Source and related guidance

[NHS images](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/images) informs the component choice and interaction guidance. The examples use shared GOV.UK primitives or original civica.uk markup, Arial typography and civica.uk assets. NHS logos and service identity are not used.

See also [cards](cards.html).

## Example artwork record

The affected example records include creator, original source, rights, purpose, intended background and alternative-text decisions. Functional SVG strokes and schematic boundaries remain separate from the flat explanatory illustration style. No official identity artwork is copied.
